WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.060
Germanium is the first element in the periodic
table,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.450
beginning at hydrogen, that’s named after
a country: it is

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.440
named after Germany. There are other elements
named after

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.580
France and Poland and America but we will
come to those

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.790
later.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.270
One of the things about Germanium and what
really makes it

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:22.670
important in the periodic table is that this
is one of the

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:28.039
elements which was unknown when Mendeleev
constructed

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:34.320
the periodic table and he predicted its existence
and when it

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.370
was found it had many of the properties that
he had

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:43.899
predicted based on the change in properties
as you go down

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:45.929
and across the periodic table.

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:49.999
So this is a small sample of germanium, named
after

00:00:49.999 --> 00:00:53.139
Germany, so you can see the wonderful shiny
surfaces.

00:00:53.139 --> 00:00:58.260
Germanium is used quite widely as a so-called
semi-

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.610
conducting material. If you look at it in
visible light it looks

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.610
like a metal.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.920
Germanium na, na, n-na na.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.530
I have used germanium mirrors in some of my
experiments.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:14.120
The lasers that I used when I was younger
had a germanium

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.479
mirror that let the light out at the front
of it and germanium

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:21.219
is used quite widely in electronics.

00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:24.380
This is quite a nice piece of germanium. Unfortunately
I broke

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.890
it somewhat earlier in my career, but you
can see very nicely

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:31.890
how this material looks like a piece of metal
but on the other

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.399
hand if you shine infrared light through it,
it’s transparent so

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:39.009
the infrared light will through but visible
light doesn’t.

